# Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in. That file is gitignored; this one is not,
# so never put a real key here.
#
# `.dev.vars` is read by wrangler (`npm run preview`) and by `next dev` through
# `initOpenNextCloudflareForDev()` in next.config.ts. In production the same two
# names are set as Workers secrets instead:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
#   npx wrangler secret put STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#
# Both are optional. With neither set, /pay still builds and renders — it says
# payments are not switched on, and the webhook refuses every event rather than
# trusting one it cannot verify.

# Test keys start sk_test_, live keys sk_live_. Use a test key until the whole
# flow has been through Stripe's test cards at least once.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace_me

# The signing secret for ONE webhook endpoint.
#
# The dashboard gives you one per endpoint. `stripe listen --forward-to
# localhost:3000/api/stripe/webhook` prints a DIFFERENT one for the forwarded
# session — when testing locally use that, not the dashboard's, or every event
# will fail the signature check.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_replace_me
